The first unbounded attempt exposed the expected semantic bottleneck: symbolic `splitSep` remains opaque, so indexing its result gets stuck. Instead of adding an execution-skipping parser rule—which would create a hard Gate A connection obligation—I’m redesigning the implementation as one fixed-semantics character loop. Its invariant can thread Horner accumulators across arbitrary digit tails, keeping parsing and control fully executable under the reference semantics.
