The loop proof closes, but proving all circularities again alongside the entry claim causes avoidable search blow-up. I’m now applying the Kit’s operational-bridge contract: preserve the seven bridge-free loop theorems in `loop-spec.k`, then admit exact-context loop-summary rules in the final definition whose match domains are identical to those proved claims. The target `spec.k` will contain only the whole-function theorem.
apply patch
