codex
A configuration-wide simplification rule is not legal in this K version. I’m using the cleaner encoding: two guarded operational rules—one digit step family and one slash-transition family—with body, return, callee-scope, and builtin-scope equality guards. Their domains are exactly the union of the seven already-proved claims (four phases plus three transitions), with no widened continuation or state frame.
